`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
**Search engine ranking patterns applied to agent routing:**
1. **Two-stage retrieval-rerank** — The core pattern. Google uses BM25 to get 1000 candidates from billions, then BERT reranks top-k. Sylveste skips stage 1 entirely, running expensive LLM judgment on 679+ agents.
2. **CTR as ground truth** — Without "clicked" (acted-on-finding) signal feeding back to ranking, the model can't improve. CASS has the session data but it's not connected to tier scoring.
3. **Position bias** — Well-documented in search: users click top results. LLMs have the same bias toward earlier-listed items. Alphabetical skill ordering creates implicit priority for "auth" over "verify".
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

